266"},{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0267"},{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0268"},{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0269"},{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0270"},{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0271"},{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0272"},{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0273"},{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0274"},{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0275"},{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0276"}]},"unitRefs":["zizhitongjian:083:s0263","zizhitongjian:083:s0264","zizhitongjian:083:s0265","zizhitongjian:083:s0266","zizhitongjian:083:s0267","zizhitongjian:083:s0268","zizhitongjian:083:s0269","zizhitongjian:083:s0270","zizhitongjian:083:s0271","zizhitongjian:083:s0272","zizhitongjian:083:s0273","zizhitongjian:083:s0274","zizhitongjian:083:s0275","zizhitongjian:083:s0276"]}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0001","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0001","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":0,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":0,"zh":"愍懷太子","en":"Crown Prince Minhuai","literal":"Crown Prince Minhuai"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0142","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0142","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":0,"zh":"喪之發也，大風雷電，幃蓋飛裂。","en":"Storm shattered funeral umbrellas.","literal":"When the hearse set out great wind and thunder came—canopies and coverings flew torn."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0143","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0143","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":1,"zh":"又為哀策曰：「皇帝臨軒，使洗馬劉務告于皇太子之殯曰：咨爾遹！","en":"They further composed a condolence text: \"The emperor facing the gallery sends Groom of the Household Liu Wu to the crown prince's lying-in-state: Ah, Yu!","literal":"They further composed a condolence text: 'The emperor facing the gallery sends Groom of the Household Liu Wu to the crown prince's lying-in-state: Ah, Yu!"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0144","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0144","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":2,"zh":"幼稟英挺，芬馨誕茂。","en":"From childhood you were outstanding, and your fine qualities flourished abundantly.","literal":"You drew from youth heroic sap, fragrance ripe at birth."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0145","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0145","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":3,"zh":"既表髫齔，高明逸秀。","en":"Even in early boyhood you displayed lofty brilliance and exceptional talents.","literal":"Already in tied hair you stood lofty and bright."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0146","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0146","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":4,"zh":"昔爾聖祖，嘉爾淑美。","en":"Your august grandfather cherished your fine virtues.","literal":"Your holy ancestor prized your fine virtue."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0147","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0147","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":5,"zh":"顯詔仍崇，名振同軌。","en":"Illustrious edicts repeatedly increased your honors; your fame resounded throughout the realm.","literal":"Illustrious edicts repeatedly increased your honors; your fame resounded throughout the realm."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0148","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0148","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":6,"zh":"是用建爾儲副，永統皇基。","en":"Therefore I established you as heir, to perpetuate the imperial foundations forever.","literal":"Therefore I established you as heir, to perpetuate the imperial foundations forever."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0149","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0149","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":7,"zh":"如何凶戾潛構，禍害如茲！","en":"How did vicious cruelty secretly weave harm like this!","literal":"How did vicious cruelty secretly weave harm like this!"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0150","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0150","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":8,"zh":"哀感和氣，痛貫四時。","en":"Sorrow moves harmonious qi; pain pierces four seasons.","literal":"Sorrow moves harmonious qi; pain pierces four seasons."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0151","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0151","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":9,"zh":"嗚呼哀哉！","en":"Alas, how grievous!","literal":"Alas, alas the sorrow!"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0152","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0152","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":10,"zh":"爾之降廢，實我不明。","en":"Your degradation was truly due to my lack of discernment.","literal":"Your degradation was truly my blindness."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0153","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0153","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":11,"zh":"牝亂沈烖，釁結禍成。","en":"A woman’s disorder brought deep calamity; hostility accumulated and disaster took shape.","literal":"Female chaos sank calamity; omens knotted into disaster."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0154","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0154","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":12,"zh":"爾之逝矣，誰百其形？","en":"Now that you have departed, who could offer a hundredfold ransom for your person?","literal":"Now that you have departed, who could offer a hundredfold ransom for your person?"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0155","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0155","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":13,"zh":"昔之申生，含枉莫訟。","en":"Long ago Shen Sheng bore false charges, with none to plead his case.","literal":"Long ago Shen Sheng bore wrong yet could not plead."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0156","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0156","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":14,"zh":"今爾之負，抱冤於東。","en":"Now you too bear unjust blame and nurse your grievance in the east.","literal":"Now your burden of grievance hugs the eastern lands."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0157","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0157","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":15,"zh":"悠悠有識，孰不哀慟！","en":"Among all who understand, who would not grieve?","literal":"Far and near anyone with insight—who fails bitter grief!"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0158","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0158","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":16,"zh":"壺關幹主，千秋悟己。","en":"The elder of Huguan remonstrated with his ruler; Qianqiu brought him to recognize his error.","literal":"The elder of Huguan remonstrated with his ruler; Qianqiu brought him to recognize his error."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0159","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0159","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":17,"zh":"異世同規，古今一理。","en":"Across different ages, the pattern is the same; past and present share one principle.","literal":"Different age, same rule—past and present one principle."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0160","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0160","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":18,"zh":"皇孫啟建，隆祚爾子。","en":"Your son has been established as imperial grandson-heir, continuing the dynastic blessing through him.","literal":"Your son has been established as imperial grandson-heir, continuing the dynastic blessing through him."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0161","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0161","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":19,"zh":"雖悴前終，庶榮後始。","en":"Though your own end was sorrowful, may the new beginning afterward be glorious.","literal":"Though front end withered, rear blossom may yet flourish."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0162","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0162","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":20,"zh":"窀穸既營，將寧爾神。","en":"Your burial chamber is now prepared, to bring your spirit peace.","literal":"Burial vault now built—we pacify your spirit."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0163","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0163","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":21,"zh":"華髦電逝，戎車雷震。","en":"Splendid plumes flash past like lightning; war chariots rumble like thunder.","literal":"Flower feathers flash like lightning; war wagons thunder."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0164","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0164","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":22,"zh":"芒芒羽蓋，翼翼縉紳。","en":"Feathered canopies stretch far and wide; the gentry advance in orderly ranks.","literal":"Vast feather-canopies; crowded sash-and-hat ranks."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0165","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0165","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":23,"zh":"同悲等痛，孰不酸辛！","en":"Courtiers weep together.","literal":"Shared grief and equal pain—who lacks bitter sorrow!"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0166","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0166","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":24,"zh":"庶光來葉，永世不泯。」","en":"May light reach posterity, never extinguished through ages.\"","literal":"May light reach posterity, never extinguished through ages.'"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0167","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0167","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":25,"zh":"諡曰湣懷。","en":"Canonized Crown Prince Minhuai.","literal":"Posthumous title Minhuai was granted."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0168","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0168","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":26,"zh":"六月己卯，葬于顯平陵。","en":"Buried sixth month at Xianping.","literal":"On jimao day of the sixth month he was buried at Xianping Mausoleum."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0169","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0169","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":27,"zh":"帝感閻纘之言，立思子台，故臣江統、陸機並作誄頌焉。","en":"Yan Zuan's plea built Son-Lament Terrace—Jiang Tong and Lu Ji wrote elegies.","literal":"Moved by Yan Zuan's words the emperor raised a Terrace of Longing for Sons; former ministers Jiang Tong and Lu Ji both composed dirges."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0170","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0170","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":28,"zh":"太子三子：虨、臧、尚，並與父同幽金墉。","en":"Three sons shared Yu's prison.","literal":"The crown prince had three sons—Bin, Zang, and Shang—all imprisoned with their father at Jinyong."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0001","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0001","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":0,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":0,"zh":"資治通鑑第083卷","en":"Zizhi Tongjian, Volume 83","literal":"Comprehensive Mirror to Aid in Government, Volume 83"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0263","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0263","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":39,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":0,"zh":"倫陰與秀謀篡位，欲先除朝望，且報宿怨，乃執張華、裴頠、解系、解結等於殿前。","en":"Lun secretly plotted usurpation with Xiu, first removing leading ministers and settling old scores; he seized Zhang Hua, Pei Wei, Xie Ji, Xie Jie, and others in the hall.","literal":"Lun secretly plotted with Xiu to usurp the throne, wishing first to remove men of court esteem and also settle old scores; he seized Zhang Hua, Pei Wei, Xie Ji, Xie Jie, and others before the hall."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0264","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0264","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":39,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":1,"zh":"華謂張林曰：「卿欲害忠臣邪？」","en":"Hua said to Zhang Lin: \"Do you mean to kill loyal ministers?\"","literal":"Hua said to Zhang Lin: \"Do you wish to harm loyal ministers?\""}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0265","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0265","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":39,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":2,"zh":"林稱詔詰之曰：「卿為宰相，太子之廢，不能死節，何也？」","en":"Lin, citing the edict, demanded: \"As chief minister, when the heir apparent was deposed why did you not die for principle?\"","literal":"Lin, claiming the edict, interrogated him: \"You were chief minister; when the Heir Apparent was deposed you could not die for principle—why?\""}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0266","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0266","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":39,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":3,"zh":"華曰：「式乾之議，臣諫事具存，可覆按也。」","en":"Hua said: \"My remonstrance at the Shiqian deliberation is on record and may be reviewed.\"","literal":"Hua said: \"On the deliberation at Shiqian my remonstrance is fully recorded and may be reviewed.\""}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0267","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0267","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":39,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":4,"zh":"林曰：「諫而不從，何不去位？」","en":"Lin said: \"If remonstrance failed, why not resign?\"","literal":"Lin said: \"If you remonstrated and were not obeyed, why not leave office?\""}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0268","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0268","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":39,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":5,"zh":"華無以對。","en":"Hua had no answer.","literal":"Hua had no reply."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0269","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0269","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":39,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":6,"zh":"遂皆斬之，仍夷三族。","en":"All were beheaded and their clans exterminated to the third degree.","literal":"They were all beheaded and their clans exterminated to the third degree."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0270","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0270","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":39,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":7,"zh":"解結女適裴氏，明日當嫁而禍起，裴氏欲認活之，女曰：「家既若此，我何以活為！」","en":"Xie Jie's daughter was to marry into the Pei clan next day when disaster struck; the Peis wished to save her; she said: \"With my house destroyed, how can I live!\"","literal":"Xie Jie's daughter was betrothed to the Pei clan; the wedding was due the next day when disaster struck; the Pei wished to claim her alive; the girl said: \"With my house thus, how can I live!\""}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0271","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0271","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":39,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":8,"zh":"亦坐死。","en":"She died as well.","literal":"She too died for it."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0272","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0272","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":39,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":9,"zh":"朝廷由是議革舊制，女不從死。","en":"The court then debated abolishing the old rule that wives and daughters die with the clan.","literal":"The court thereupon debated abolishing the old rule that daughters follow their kin to death."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0273","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0273","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":39,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":10,"zh":"甲午，倫坐端門，遣尚書和郁持節送賈庶人於金墉；","en":"On jiawu Lun sat at the Duan Gate and sent He Yu with credentials to convey the deposed empress to Jinyong;","literal":"On the day jiawu Lun sat at the Duan Gate and sent the Masters of Writing He Yu with credentials to convey the deposed Jia commoner to Jinyong;"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0274","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0274","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":39,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":11,"zh":"誅劉振、董猛、孫慮、程據等；","en":"Liu Zhen, Dong Meng, Sun Lv, Cheng Ju, and others were executed;","literal":"Liu Zhen, Dong Meng, Sun Lv, Cheng Ju, and others were executed;"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0275","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0275","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":39,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":12,"zh":"司徒王戎及內外官坐張、裴親黨黜免者甚眾。","en":"Minister over the Masses Wang Rong and many inner and outer officials were dismissed as kin to Zhang and Pei.","literal":"the Minister over the Masses Wang Rong and inner and outer officials dismissed as kin to Zhang and Pei were very numerous."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0276","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0276","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":39,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":13,"zh":"閻纘撫張華屍慟哭曰：「早語君遜位而不肯，今果不免，命也！」","en":"Yan Xun stroked Zhang Hua's corpse and wailed: \"I urged you to resign and you would not; now you could not escape—fate!\"","literal":"Yan Xun stroked Zhang Hua's corpse and wailed: \"I told you early to yield your post and you would not; now you could not escape—fate!\""}},{"kind":"person-record","key":"jinshu:053:p066","value":{"localId":"jinshu:053:p066","preferredNameSuggestion":{"en":"Yan Zuan","zh":"閻纘","pinyin":"Yan Zuan"},"historicity":"historical","descriptorSuggestion":"Official whose words moved emperor","identityHints":{"nativePlaces":[],"relatedLocalPeople":["jinshu:053:p002"],"activeDateHints":["AD 300"],"polityHints":["Western Jin","晉"]},"book":"jinshu","chapter":"053","promptVersion":7,"sourceUnitRefs":["jinshu:053:s0169"],"chapterPinRef":"jinshu:053","aliasesAndNameKeys":[{"key":"en:yan zuan","language":"en","value":"Yan Zuan","kinds":["personal-name","preferred"],"sources":["jinshu:053:c0233","preferred"],"blocking":true},{"key":"zh:閻纘","language":"zh","value":"閻纘","kinds":["personal-name","preferred"],"sources":["jinshu:053:c0233","preferred"],"blocking":true}],"governingBlockRefs":["jinshu:053:block:9"],"currentCanonicalPersonId":"per_7JKZA0CW7MJAZY39JWHF","inboundSourceUnitRefs":[],"inboundGoverningBlockRefs":[]}},{"kin